{"nodes": [{"type": "group", "id": "b973867b4fe24e6b", "x": -2444, "y": -1110, "width": 1255, "height": 1237, "color": "#89dceb", "label": "Comment \u00e7a marche", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "group", "id": "20765cb2f3cc4d11", "x": -680, "y": -2437, "width": 1360, "height": 1505, "color": "#cba6f7", "label": "Carbone et oxyg\u00e8ne", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "group", "id": "e4c36150cbd54ef3", "x": 994, "y": 302, "width": 930, "height": 1080, "color": "#cba6f7", "label": "Micro-organisme photosynth\u00e9tique", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "group", "id": "1c51e25a525f49ee", "x": -1566, "y": 979, "width": 480, "height": 710, "color": "#cba6f7", "label": "\u00c9volution (biologie)", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "group", "id": "78cbd7adb0b14b05", "x": 1685, "y": 1685, "width": 550, "height": 390, "color": "#f38ba8", "label": "\u00c0 ne pas confondre", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "group", "id": "8ed3200a5bd14828", "x": -240, "y": 2437, "width": 480, "height": 300, "color": "#f5c2e7", "label": "Sources", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "text", "id": "4162a39d1e264338", "x": -2404, "y": -550, "width": 450, "height": 450, "color": "#a6e3a1", "text": "**Graphique**\n\n```tikz\n\n\\begin{tikzpicture}\n\\begin{axis}[\n    axis lines=middle,\n    grid=both,\n    domain=0:5,\n    samples=200,\n    xlabel={$x$},\n    ylabel={$f(x)$},\n    width=10cm,\n    height=8cm\n]\n\\addplot[blue, thick] {exp(-1*x^2)};\n\\end{axis}\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n\n```"}, {"type": "text", "id": "d3fa2a6ba7e14d9e", "x": -1924, "y": -550, "width": 280, "height": 170, "color": null, "text": "### assimilats\n\nlumi\u00e8re, chlorophylle, H2O, CO2 \u2192 H+, e-, O2, assimilats (feuille)"}, {"type": "text", "id": "5be2c8e7300340f2", "x": -1924, "y": -1030, "width": 280, "height": 170, "color": "#89dceb", "text": "### G3P\n\n\u00e9nergie emmagasin\u00e9e \u2192 G3P, ADP, Pi, NADP+"}, {"type": "text", "id": "11b5fa0479ad45cd", "x": -1509, "y": -790, "width": 280, "height": 170, "color": "#89dceb", "text": "### ADP\n\n\u00e9nergie emmagasin\u00e9e \u2192 G3P, ADP, Pi, NADP+"}, {"type": "text", "id": "102d45895b854e3c", "x": -1509, "y": -311, "width": 280, "height": 170, "color": "#89dceb", "text": "### NADP+\n\n\u00e9nergie emmagasin\u00e9e \u2192 G3P, ADP, Pi, NADP+"}, {"type": "text", "id": "f9b0b995321e47f5", "x": -1924, "y": -58, "width": 280, "height": 145, "color": "#89dceb", "text": "### (CH2O)n\n\nCO2, AH2, photons \u2192 (CH2O)n, AO"}, {"type": "text", "id": "f472ad7d3cec427a", "x": -640, "y": -2037, "width": 400, "height": 245, "color": null, "text": "### Dioxyg\u00e8ne\n\nChez les plantes , les algues , les cyanobact\u00e9ries et plusieurs taxons de bact\u00e9ries ( bact\u00e9ries sulfureuses vertes , bact\u00e9ries non sulfureuses vertes ), la photosynth\u00e8se lib\u00e8re du dioxyg\u00e8ne O 2 , au cours de la photosynth\u00e8se oxyg\u00e9nique."}, {"type": "link", "id": "81666d6741b54f8e", "x": -640, "y": -2357, "width": 400, "height": 300, "color": "#cba6f7", "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Masse_volumique_dioxyg%C3%A8ne.svg/500px-Masse_volumique_dioxyg%C3%A8ne.svg.png"}, {"type": "text", "id": "109ae7d96e084129", "x": -190, "y": -2037, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "### Glucide\n\nOn parle de \u00ab plantes en C 3 \u00bb en r\u00e9f\u00e9rence au 3-phosphoglyc\u00e9rate , mol\u00e9cule \u00e0 trois atomes de carbone form\u00e9e par condensation du dioxyde de carbone CO 2 sur du ribulose-1,5-bisphosphate par la Rubisco : + CO 2 + H 2 O \u2192 2 D -ribulose-1,5-bisphosphate 3-phospho- D -glyc\u00e9rate Carboxylase/oxyg\u00e9nase..."}, {"type": "text", "id": "812350ff8dee4552", "x": -190, "y": -1617, "width": 400, "height": 245, "color": "#cba6f7", "text": "#### Carbone\n\nDans la photosynth\u00e8se oxyg\u00e9nique, l'eau est le donneur d'\u00e9lectrons, dont la dissociation lib\u00e8re de l' oxyg\u00e8ne tandis que de l'eau est reform\u00e9e \u00e0 partir d'un atome d'oxyg\u00e8ne du dioxyde de carbone : 2 n CO 2 + 4 n H 2 O + photons \u2192 2(CH 2 O) n + 2 n O 2 + 2 n H 2 O ."}, {"type": "text", "id": "f54d944a7d0d4912", "x": 240, "y": -2037, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "### Chlorophylle b\n\nLa chlorophylle b est une forme de chlorophylle de couleur vert olive qui absorbe essentiellement la lumi\u00e8re bleue et qui est davantage soluble en milieu aqueux que la chlorophylle a en raison de la pr\u00e9sence d'un groupement carbonyle dans sa structure.\nLa chlorophylle b n'est pas un donneur..."}, {"type": "text", "id": "649ac70dbc6f45a9", "x": -640, "y": -1342, "width": 200, "height": 370, "color": null, "text": "#### Cas particuliers de photosynth\u00e8se\n\nCas particuliers de photosynth\u00e8se Plante au microscope \u00e9lectrique Animaux et photosynth\u00e8se La limace de mer , Elysia chlorotica , est le premier animal d\u00e9couvert capable d'utiliser la photosynth\u00e8se pour produire de l'\u00e9nergie."}, {"type": "text", "id": "86d2e21105e44431", "x": 1034, "y": 702, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "### Organisme (physiologie)\n\nUn organisme (du grec organon, \u00ab instrument \u00bb), ou organisme vivant, est, en biologie et en \u00e9cologie, un syst\u00e8me vivant complexe, organis\u00e9 et est le produit de variations successives au cours de l'\u00e9volution. Il est constitu\u00e9 d'une ou plusieurs cellules vivantes (on parle alors, respectivement,..."}, {"type": "link", "id": "5ca6d9d4b33a48a1", "x": 1034, "y": 382, "width": 400, "height": 300, "color": "#cba6f7", "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Adolphe_Millot_algues.jpg/500px-Adolphe_Millot_algues.jpg"}, {"type": "text", "id": "6c681fe164f5450d", "x": 1484, "y": 702, "width": 400, "height": 245, "color": null, "text": "### Micro-organisme\n\nCertains micro-organismes peuvent utiliser \u00e0 la place le cycle de Krebs inverse [ 1 ] , tandis que d'autres poss\u00e8dent des voies de fixation du carbone diff\u00e9rentes telles que la voie de Wood-Ljungdahl ou encore le cycle du 3-hydroxypropionate et ses diverses variantes."}, {"type": "text", "id": "c76611a32a794d0e", "x": 1484, "y": 1097, "width": 400, "height": 245, "color": "#cba6f7", "text": "#### Algue\n\nChez les plantes , les algues , les cyanobact\u00e9ries et plusieurs taxons de bact\u00e9ries ( bact\u00e9ries sulfureuses vertes , bact\u00e9ries non sulfureuses vertes ), la photosynth\u00e8se lib\u00e8re du dioxyg\u00e8ne O 2 , au cours de la photosynth\u00e8se oxyg\u00e9nique."}, {"type": "text", "id": "1e46ef11535244e6", "x": -1526, "y": 1379, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "### \u00c9volution (biologie)\n\nEn biologie, l\u2019\u00e9volution est la transformation du monde vivant au cours du temps, qui se manifeste par des changements ph\u00e9notypiques des organismes \u00e0 travers les g\u00e9n\u00e9rations. Ces changements g\u00e9n\u00e9ralement graduels (mais pouvant \u00eatre rapides ou lents) peuvent aboutir, \u00e0 partir d\u2019une seule esp\u00e8ce..."}, {"type": "link", "id": "79d405a2539e4bb9", "x": -1526, "y": 1059, "width": 400, "height": 300, "color": "#cba6f7", "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Tree_of_life_by_Haeckel.jpg/500px-Tree_of_life_by_Haeckel.jpg"}, {"type": "text", "id": "15b5ff1c059e4ce4", "x": 1725, "y": 1765, "width": 220, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "#### \u2260 respiration cellulaire\n\nLa photosynth\u00e8se produit O\u2082 et glucose \u00e0 partir de CO\u2082 et lumi\u00e8re. La respiration cellulaire fait l'inverse : consomme O\u2082 et glucose pour produire de l'\u00e9nergie."}, {"type": "text", "id": "88991fe416084a0a", "x": 1975, "y": 1765, "width": 220, "height": 220, "color": null, "text": "#### \u2260 chimiosynth\u00e8se\n\nLa chimiosynth\u00e8se utilise l'\u00e9nergie chimique au lieu de la lumi\u00e8re pour produire de la mati\u00e8re organique."}, {"type": "text", "id": "5225d988e2704861", "x": -200, "y": 2517, "width": 400, "height": 180, "color": "#f5c2e7", "text": "Science (revue)"}], "edges": [{"id": "6b78972cc2544f8c", "fromNode": "d3fa2a6ba7e14d9e", "fromSide": "top", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "5be2c8e7300340f2", "toSide": "bottom", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "cycle d'assimilation du carbone"}, {"id": "968864d54a6a4349", "fromNode": "5be2c8e7300340f2", "fromSide": "right", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "11b5fa0479ad45cd", "toSide": "left", "toEnd": null, "color": "#89dceb", "label": "cycle d'assimilation du carbone"}, {"id": "a4048e38274c4408", "fromNode": "11b5fa0479ad45cd", "fromSide": "bottom", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "102d45895b854e3c", "toSide": "top", "toEnd": null, "color": "#89dceb", "label": "cycle d'assimilation du carbone"}, {"id": "8f8e0ee336fe4115", "fromNode": "102d45895b854e3c", "fromSide": "left", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "f9b0b995321e47f5", "toSide": "right", "toEnd": null, "color": "#89dceb", "label": "produit"}, {"id": "b1c0fb43eb5f4050", "fromNode": "109ae7d96e084129", "fromSide": "bottom", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "812350ff8dee4552", "toSide": "top", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "composant de"}, {"id": "e39d2f9812d442b7", "fromNode": "6c681fe164f5450d", "fromSide": "bottom", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "c76611a32a794d0e", "toSide": "top", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "composante de"}, {"id": "016c85537284438e", "fromNode": "e4c36150cbd54ef3", "fromSide": "left", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "1c51e25a525f49ee", "toSide": "right", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "contient"}, {"id": "89094ad6ce5b4fd5", "fromNode": "e4c36150cbd54ef3", "fromSide": "top", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "20765cb2f3cc4d11", "toSide": "bottom", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "Micro-organisme photosynth\u00e9tique \u2192 Carbone et oxyg\u00e8ne"}, {"id": "2b2a7dd9151e4eb6", "fromNode": "1c51e25a525f49ee", "fromSide": "top", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "20765cb2f3cc4d11", "toSide": "bottom", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "\u00c9volution (biologie) \u2192 Carbone et oxyg\u00e8ne"}]}